From 0ce52d71beaff17c9d7d853beb33249c10cfc518 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shircomay <112399495+shircomay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:50:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(export): write a Markdown transcript next to each
 recording
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds an opt-in `.md` transcript written beside the `.srt`, and an
"Export Transcript (.md)…" command next to "Export Subtitles (.srt)…".

- MarkdownTranscriptExporter adapts a Recording to MilaKit's
  ParagraphTranscriptFormatter and owns the YAML front matter and file I/O.
  Speaker labels use displaySpeakerName, so the .md, the UI and the .srt
  agree.
- MarkdownExportSettings (markdownExport.* keys): sidecar on/off (default
  off), paragraph timestamps (default on), and what vault notes contain.
- TranscriptExporter.writeSRT also writes the sidecar, which covers every
  RecordingStore call site. RecordingStore removes the .md with the .srt, and
  rewrites it when a completed recording is renamed or retitled.
- Settings > Storage gets a "Markdown transcripts" section with a one-shot
  "Write Markdown for existing recordings" backfill.

The .srt is still written: the subtitle-video feature reads it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
